# Authenticated Windows XP SP3 x86 kernel/HAL export baselines, for the
# import gate's hlprx86 profile: xhcihlpr.sys, the x86 helper (design record
# 18 section 15.11), which loads on Windows 2000 SP4, XP SP3, Vista SP2 and 7
# SP1 x86 and is gated against every kernel and HAL each of them can run.
#
# Source: the owner's own Windows XP Professional SP3 OEM medium (volume
# GRTMPOEM_EN, the medium legal-provenance.md section 4 names for XP SP3's
# usbport.sys), measured 2026-10-14 (task 38.3). XP SP3 ships the four
# kernels - uniprocessor and multiprocessor, each without and with PAE - and
# seven HALs, all inside I386\SP3.CAB; ntoskrnl.exe, ntkrnlmp.exe and the
# HALs are also loose and compressed in I386\ (NTOSKRNL.EX_, HAL.DL_ ...),
# and the loose copies expand to the same bytes (ntoskrnl.exe and hal.dll
# compared 2026-10-14). The PAE kernels exist only in the cab, so every row
# is taken from it.
#
# **PACKED names a member of I386\SP3.CAB**, not a file in I386\: that is
# the difference from win2k-baselines.expected, and
# scripts\import-gate\extract-target-baselines.ps1 -WinXpIso reads it so.
# The import descriptor names NTOSKRNL.EXE or HAL.DLL whichever image the
# loader binds it to, so every row must export each pair the helper imports.
#
# Format, identical to win2k-baselines.expected:
#   PACKED OUTPUT PROVIDER VERSION LENGTH SHA256
# VERSION is the number before the build-lab tag ("5.1.2600.5512
# (xpsp.080413-2111)" in each file's resource), as winxp64-baselines.expected
# records it.

